### Lab 7 - requests for the IntelliJ HTTP client (or copy them as curl -i commands)
@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. List (200, JSON array of BookResponse)
GET {{host}}/api/books

### 2. Filter by author (200)
GET {{host}}/api/books?author=Joshua Bloch

### 3. Find one (200)
GET {{host}}/api/books/1

### 4. Find a missing one (404, application/problem+json)
GET {{host}}/api/books/999

### 5. Create a valid book (201 + Location header)
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Refactoring",
  "author": "Martin Fowler",
  "year": 2018,
  "genre": "PROGRAMMING"
}

### 6. Create with an empty title (400, problem detail from the base class)
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "author": "Martin Fowler",
  "year": 2018,
  "genre": "PROGRAMMING"
}

### 7. Create a duplicate (409) - this book is already in the seed data
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Effective Java",
  "author": "Joshua Bloch",
  "year": 2018,
  "genre": "PROGRAMMING"
}

### 8. Unreadable body / unknown genre (400)
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Dune",
  "author": "Frank Herbert",
  "year": 1965,
  "genre": "NOT_A_GENRE"
}

### 9. Update (200)
PUT {{host}}/api/books/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Clean Code",
  "author": "Robert Martin",
  "year": 2009,
  "genre": "PROGRAMMING"
}

### 10. Update a missing book (404)
PUT {{host}}/api/books/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Ghost",
  "author": "Nobody",
  "year": 2000,
  "genre": "FICTION"
}

### 11. Delete (204, no body)
DELETE {{host}}/api/books/1

### 12. The same DELETE again (404 - our decision, see BookService.delete)
DELETE {{host}}/api/books/1

### 13. OpenAPI document and Swagger UI (open in the browser)
GET {{host}}/v3/api-docs
